														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3784648">
									

<p>As much as the end was funny, I actually disliked the behavior of the Foundation on this one, in several places.</p>
<p>The compliance of JaJa with the Foundation, the history of betrayal from other user, those where good readings.</p>
<p>Operation Aggressive Networking, though, is completely off for the Foundation to me. I'm not a fan of SCP weaponization, and I hardly see the Foundation putting this much in use of an anomaly without even testing it properly.</p>
<p>It is also very unlikely that they would do so messily. They are conducting huge military expeditions in front of civilians that could be spying on then, is that serious?</p>
<p>Maybe this could work better with involvement of other GoI with more aggressive behavior, like GOC or CI, but as a Foundation operation it seemed too off for me.</p>

